  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** The company is exhibiting operational momentum, with accelerating revenue growth and marking its best quarterly gross margin in years. A recent acquisition is already contributing, as surplus inventory was converted to sales without price discounting, pointing to healthy underlying demand. The firm is moving toward positive EBITDA, a key inflection point, though available commentary provides little detail on competitive pressures, end-market trends, or macroeconomic influences.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership reaffirmed full-year guidance while targeting near-term EBITDA breakeven and swiftly unlocked value from the CSI acquisition by monetizing surplus stock. Despite these operational strides, market sentiment remains deeply skeptical: the stock trades at distressed levels, and the lone analyst rating stands at Sell. This disconnect suggests a credibility gap, with execution progress yet to translate into investor confidence.",
